  "design": [
    "Core fixed observed backings preserve physical address across snapshots, copying snapshots independently; ordinary buffers retain COW.",
    "Pinning an externally shared zero store accounts actual newly owned allocation once. Core owns storage and alignment; Node owns Buffer ABI/pool policy.",
    "Native allocation creates a real ArrayBuffer with initialized bytes. Unsafe permits zero initialization. No synthetic pointers or zero-fill toggles.",
    "One shared private pool state handles from(strings/arraylike) and copyBytesFrom, actual mark-untransferable, physical base alignment and reentrant cursor semantics.",
    "Original latest Node library remains guest code over genuine Rust primitives; no Node guest execution."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Goal remains open. Latest complete stable full1783/5015 is from older c4ad13141, not this source. Do not add selected gains to full totals.",
    "Remaining selected broadcast-waiter-cleanup times out unchanged at30s; own smaller-count diagnostic completes without consumers. This is not retention proof.",
    "allocUnsafe/concat remain legacy unpooled and latest aligned public allocation arguments are not yet implemented.",
    "No setDetachKey export until complete real detach-key semantics exist.",
    "Fixed-work diagnostic does not establish a speed claim; compilation/full inventory overlap precludes isolated timing attribution.",
    "Core before latest accounting passed649; linker disk exhaustion was retained and recovered using only failed owned temporary plus byte-identical immutable binary hardlink dedup."
  ],
